*CHAOS CONTROL — the decisive experiment
----------------------------------------
sensitivity.py: numpy golden re-run with float64-accumulated GEMMs (a
different but equally valid fp32-level ordering) decays the SAME way:
  b31 100.000  b32 100.000  b33 100.000  b34 100.000  b35  99.981
  b36  93.590  b37  69.085  b38  52.170 (83.998 <=1step)
The GPU's 49.209/81.963 sits inside the golden-vs-golden-reordered envelope.
The 8x full-288-token attention chain is chaotically sensitive to fp32 GEMM
accumulation order: NO fp32 implementation can bit-match the numpy golden at
b38 >=99.9% (M7 reached the same conclusion for single-block scores via its
float64 control). This is NOT a porting regression: b31/b32 are bit-exact and
every kernel/rounding point matches the M7-validated implementation.

DECODER/HEAD — cascade proof
----------------------------
hybrid.py: golden decoder fed with the GPU's ACTUAL b38 dump still diverges
from the GPU decoder at b39 (2.842% bitmatch): window attention compounds
ANY seed over 30 blocks. Decoder kernels are byte-identical to the stem/
encoder kernels that pass 100% at b4ds/b22ds, so their math is validated;
boundary compares downstream of the global family are chaos-inherited, not
kernel errors.

